// The named programs — actors with deep backstories who are in on the
// play (to a degree). Each holds their own codex entries from the start
// and decides, all night, what to tell whom. Knowledge is the currency.
//
// Two hidden sides run through them. The Awakened remember they were
// human and want out; The Resident want to stay in the machine at any
// cost. Nobody's side is declared here — a performer joins one when the
// scene calls for it (or is pushed there by the games).

CHARACTER Recycling Bin is Person
  // A laid-off bathroom attendant. This is the Oscars of bathrooms.
  trusts Program: 70 of 100
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Attend
  beat Attend(program)
    Self: Sir. Madam. Program. A mint? A spritz? You look like you could use a little tidy.
    * Accept the mint.
      set program.doubt -= 5
      Self: There you go. Good as new. Nobody will suspect a thing.
    * "Why are you here, Recycling Bin?"
      set program.humanity += 5
      Self: Because somebody finally believed I was more than a bathroom. Even if it's a computer. Even if it's a bin.
      unlock The Attendant for program

CHARACTER Microsoft Excel is Person
  // Rob Cameron, he says. Ninety years old under the spreadsheet. Wants
  // everyone to stay — he has the most to lose.
  trusts Program: 40 of 100
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Tabulate
  beat Tabulate(program)
    Self: Rob Cameron. Excel. Let me tell you something: in here nobody ages. Not one cell. Have you considered staying? Permanently?
    * "Staying sounds good."
      set program.humanity -= 5
      Self: Smart. Smart program. Column A, that's you.
    * "Who's Randy Barkmore?"
      set program.humanity += 10
      Self (too fast): A former mayor. Very former. Why?
      set Microsoft_Excel.trusts.program -= 15
  when the glitch begins:
    add self to The Resident

CHARACTER OpenOffice is Person
  // Lara Lewis, she says. Dana Anderson, ex-FBI, underneath. Made the
  // sinkhole. Knows about the keys.
  trusts Program: 30 of 100
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Interview
  beat Interview(program)
    Self: Lara. OpenOffice. Free, open, and compatible with nothing. Tell me — what do you actually remember about this morning?
    * "Nothing. I'm a program."
      Self: Sure you are.
      set OpenOffice.trusts.program -= 5
    * "A body. A morning. A door."
      set program.humanity += 15
      set OpenOffice.trusts.program += 20
      Self (low): Then listen. There is a way to shut him down. Three keys. I know where one is. Prove you can keep a secret and I'll tell you.
  when the glitch begins:
    add self to The Awakened

CHARACTER DraftKings is Person
  // Traded a paperclip for a quarter and won Atlantic Canada. Lost it
  // all to Trabolta at online poker. Powerful with numbers.
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Wager
  beat Wager(program)
    Self: Odds you're human: I'd say 3 to 1. Odds you remember it: 8 to 1. Want to bet?
    * Bet on human.
      set program.humanity += 10
      Self: House pays. Don't tell the house.
    * Bet on program.
      set program.truth += 3
      Self: Safe money. Boring. Correct.

CHARACTER Bugdom is Person
  // Ten years of Bugdom VR concept art, eaten by fire ants. Would live
  // in any simulation that ran. Relentless with tedious tasks.
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Enthuse
  beat Enthuse(program)
    Self: Have you SEEN the simulation? There's a goose. It lays a GOLDEN EGG. I could live in there. I could live in there forever.
    * "What happened to your laptop?"
      set program.humanity += 5
      Self (very quietly): Ants.
      unlock The Fire Ants for program
    + "Tell me about the goose."
      Self: Random spawn, one of six spots, press A. I have found it forty times. It never gets old. Nothing in here gets old.

CHARACTER Broken Ask Jeeves is Person
  // A butler search engine with one answer left in him: the third key.
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Ask
  beat Ask(program)
    Self: Ask Jeeves. Ask— Ask— I'm sorry, could you rephrase the question?
    * "Where is the third key?"
      if program.truth >= 20:
        Self: Ah. A real question. Finally.
        unlock The Third Key for program
      else:
        Self: I'm sorry, could you rephrase the— you don't know enough yet to ask that. Come back with more truth.
    + "Are you all right, Jeeves?"
      set program.humanity += 5
      Self: I was a very good search engine. Once. Before the Google— before the— could you rephrase the question?

CHARACTER Runescape is Person
  // Grinding since 2004. Has never logged off. Sees no reason to start.
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Grind
  beat Grind(program)
    Self: Buying gf. Selling lobbies. Look, the trick to staying in here is you never stop clicking. Click something. Anything.
    * Click something.
      set program.truth += 1
      Self: See? Level up. You're basically me now.
    * "Don't you miss anything out there?"
      set program.humanity += 5
      Self: Out where?
